==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*weǵʰ-}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*vezti}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*weǵʰ-}}. Cognate with {{cog|la|vehō}}, {{cog|sa|वहति}}, {{cog|ang|wegan}} ({{cog|en|weigh}}).

{{sense|to be lucky}} Compare typologically {{m+|la|fortūna}} (akin to {{m|la|ferō}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|везти́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-везти.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-везти.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{homophones|ru|вести́}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|везти́|impf|pf=повезти́}}

# to [[convey]], to [[carry]] (by vehicle), to [[deliver]], to [[transport]]
#: {{syn|ru|транспорти́ровать}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=2018|author=w:ru:Владимир Сорокин<t:{{w|Vladimir Sorokin}}>|title=Красная пирамида|chapter=|location=Москва|publisher=w:ru:[[АСТ (издательство)|Издательство АСТ]]|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Max Lawton|title2=Red Pyramid|location2=New York|publisher2=w:New York Review Books|year2=2024|page2=|pageurl2=|text=В пода́рок он '''вёз''' буты́лку шампа́нского и то́мик стихо́в Уо́лта Уи́тмена в перево́де Корне́я Чуко́вского.|t=He '''was bearing''' a bottle of champagne and a book of poems by Walt Whitman translated by Korney Chukovsky as gifts.}}
# {{lb|ru|impersonal}} to be [[lucky]], to have [[luck]], to [[work out]] for, to [[succeed]], to be [[successful]] {{+obj|ru|dat<for someone> + inf<to do something>}}
#: {{syn|ru|уда́чливый<t:lucky>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|Па́ше [[и]] Са́ше [[не]] '''везёт''' [[сего́дня]]|t=Pasha and Sasha are having no luck today.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[дурак|дурака́м]] [[всегда́]] '''везёт'''|t=fools are always lucky}}
#: {{pf|ru|повезти́}}

